SPECS={
1:{'ar':'بعد want to نستخدم الفعل بصيغته الأساسية. الرغبة لا تعني وجود التزام.','en':'Use want to followed by the base verb to express a desire. A desire is not necessarily an obligation.','tags':['رغبات','خطط','تعبير شخصي','daily','desire'],'compare':['want to رغبة، need to حاجة، have to ضرورة أو التزام، would like to ألطف في الطلب.','Want to expresses desire; need to focuses on need; have to expresses necessity; would like to is a more polite request.'],'gap':['I want to ___ English.','learn','learning','learns'],'fill':['She ___ to learn English.',['wants'],'مع she نضيف s إلى want، ولا نضيفها إلى الفعل بعد to.','With she, use wants. The verb after to stays in its base form.'],'negative':"I don't want to leave yet.",'bad':"I don't want leaving yet.",'meaning':['ما الغرض الأساسي من I want to؟','التعبير عن رغبة','التعبير عن منع','سرد عادة سابقة'],'context':['تريد بدء هواية جديدة. أي عبارة تعبّر عن الرغبة؟','I want to learn photography.','I have to show my passport.','I used to play football.'],'advanced':[('Want + object + to-infinitive','يمكن أن نضيف مفعولًا قبل to عندما نريد من شخص آخر فعل شيء.','Add an object before to when you want another person to do something.','I want you to check this.','I want you ___ this.','to check',['checking','check']),('Would rather vs want to','بعد would rather يأتي الفعل دون to، مع أن want to يأخذ to.','Would rather takes a bare infinitive; want to takes a to-infinitive.',"I'd rather stay home.","I'd rather ___ home.",'stay',['to stay','staying'])]},
13:{'ar':'بعد need to نستخدم الفعل الأساسي للتعبير عن حاجة. مع he أو she تصبح needs to.','en':'Need to takes the base verb and expresses a need. Use needs to with he or she.','tags':['احتياجات','مساعدة','حل مشكلات','needs','daily'],'compare':['need to يركز على الحاجة، وhave to على الضرورة أو الالتزام؛ قد يصحان في الموقف نفسه.','Need to emphasizes need; have to emphasizes necessity or obligation. Both may be possible in the same situation.'],'gap':['I need to ___ some water.','drink','drinking','drinks'],'fill':['He ___ to charge his phone.',['needs'],'تأخذ need حرف s مع he، ويبقى charge في الصيغة الأساسية.','Use needs with he; charge remains the base verb.'],'negative':"You don't need to bring anything.",'bad':"You don't need bringing anything.",'meaning':['ماذا تعني You don’t need to hurry؟','لا حاجة إلى الاستعجال','يُمنع عليك الاستعجال','أنت تسرع دائمًا'],'context':['هاتفك فارغ البطارية قبل الخروج. أي عبارة تصف الحاجة؟','I need to charge my phone.','I used to live here.','This is my friend.'],'advanced':[('Needn’t + base verb','يمكن استخدام needn’t مع الفعل دون to للتعبير عن عدم الضرورة.','Needn’t takes the bare infinitive and expresses lack of necessity.',"You needn't wait.","You needn't ___ for me.",'wait',['to wait','waiting']),('Need doing: passive meaning','The door needs painting تعني أن الباب يحتاج إلى أن يُطلى. هذه صيغة ذات معنى مبني للمجهول.','Needs painting means needs to be painted; the -ing form has a passive meaning here.','The door needs painting.','The door needs ___ before winter.','painting',['paint','to painting'])]},
2:{'ar':'have to يتبعه فعل أساسي. مع he أو she نستخدم has to، وفي الماضي had to.','en':'Have to is followed by the base verb. Use has to with he or she and had to for the past.','tags':['التزام','ضرورة','مسؤوليات','عمل','obligation'],'compare':['don’t have to يعني عدم الضرورة؛ mustn’t يعني المنع.','Don’t have to means there is no obligation; mustn’t means something is prohibited.'],'gap':['I have to ___ my work.','finish','finishing','finished'],'fill':['She ___ to leave now.',['has'],'نستخدم has مع she في الحاضر.','Use has with she in the present.'],'negative':"You don't have to work tomorrow.",'bad':"You don't have work tomorrow.",'meaning':['ماذا تعني You don’t have to come؟','لست مضطرًا إلى الحضور','ممنوع أن تحضر','يجب أن تحضر'],'context':['قواعد الموقع تلزم الزوار بارتداء خوذة. اختر التعبير المناسب.','I have to wear a helmet.','I want to read a novel.','I used to work here.'],'advanced':[('Past necessity','للتعبير عن التزام في الماضي نستخدم had to، لا musted.','Use had to for past necessity; must has no form musted.','I had to leave early.','Yesterday I ___ leave early.','had to',['musted','have to']),('No obligation vs prohibition','لا تخلط غياب الالتزام بالمنع الصريح؛ معنى السؤال يحدد الاختيار.','Distinguish absence of obligation from prohibition; context determines the answer.',"You mustn't touch this wire.",'Touching this wire is forbidden. You ___ touch it.',"mustn't",["don't have to","don't need to"])]},
3:{'ar':'I’d like to اختصار I would like to، وهي صيغة مهذبة للرغبة أو الطلب. يلي to فعل أساسي.','en':'I’d like to means I would like to. It is a polite way to express a wish or request and takes the base verb.','tags':['تهذيب','طلبات','خدمات','سفر','polite'],'compare':['I’d like a room: بعد like اسم. I’d like to book: بعد like to فعل.','Use would like + noun for a thing and would like to + verb for an action.'],'gap':["I'd like to ___ a room.",'book','booking','books'],'fill':['Would you like ___ join us?',['to'],'نستخدم to قبل الفعل join بعد would like.','Use to before join after would like.'],'negative':"I'd like to ask a question.",'bad':"I'd like asking a question.",'meaning':['ماذا تعبّر I’d like to عن نفسها عادةً؟','رغبة أو طلب مهذب','عادة في الماضي','منع قانوني'],'context':['أنت عند استقبال الفندق وتود حجز غرفة بأدب.','I would like to book a room.','I used to book rooms.','I have no room.'],'advanced':[('Would like + object + to','يمكن تحديد الشخص الذي نود منه تنفيذ الفعل بوضع المفعول قبل to.','Place an object before to to say who you want to perform the action.',"I'd like you to explain it.","I'd like you ___ it.",'to explain',['explain','explaining']),('Would have liked to','would have liked to تصف رغبة سابقة، وغالبًا تشير إلى أنها لم تتحقق في السياق.','Would have liked to describes a past wish, often one that was not fulfilled in context.',"I would have liked to join you.",'I would have liked ___ you yesterday.','to join',['joining','join'])]},
4:{'ar':'بعد can يأتي الفعل دون to ودون إضافة s. نبدأ سؤال الاستئذان بـ Can I.','en':'Can takes the bare infinitive, without to or an -s ending. Can I is a common permission request.','tags':['استئذان','مساعدة','طلبات','أسئلة','permission'],'compare':['Can I لطلب الإذن أو الخدمة. Could I صيغة أكثر تهذيبًا غالبًا.','Can I asks permission or requests a service. Could I is often more polite.'],'gap':['Can I ___ a question?','ask','to ask','asking'],'fill':['Can she ___ this room?',['use'],'بعد can نستخدم use دون s حتى مع she.','Use the base verb use after can, even with she.'],'negative':'Can I sit here?','bad':'Can I to sit here?','meaning':['ما وظيفة Can I borrow your pen?','طلب الاستئذان','وصف عادة سابقة','التنبؤ بالمستقبل'],'context':['تريد استعارة قلم من زميلك، فماذا تقول؟','Can I borrow your pen?','I used to borrow pens.','It takes a pen.'],'advanced':[('Could I for polite permission','Could I صيغة مهذبة لطلب الإذن في الحاضر، وليست دائمًا سؤالًا عن الماضي.','Could I can ask politely for present permission; it is not always about past ability.','Could I leave a little early?','Could I ___ a little early?','leave',['to leave','leaving']),('Can vs be able to','في تركيب will نستخدم be able to لأن الأفعال الناقصة لا تتتابع بهذه الصورة.','After will, use be able to; modal verbs do not combine as will can.','I will be able to help.','Tomorrow I will ___ help.','be able to',['can','could'])]},
5:{'ar':'This is للمفرد القريب. These are للجمع القريب. بعد is يمكن أن يأتي اسم أو وصف أو تركيب أطول.','en':'This is refers to a nearby singular item. These are refers to nearby plural items. Is can be followed by a noun, description, or longer complement.','tags':['تعريف','إشارة','تعارف','منزل','demonstratives'],'compare':['this / these للقريب، وthat / those للبعيد؛ يطابق الفعل المفرد أو الجمع.','This/these refer to near items; that/those refer to distant items. Match singular and plural agreement.'],'gap':['This ___ my house.','is','are','am'],'fill':['These ___ my books.',['are'],'These جمع، لذلك تحتاج are.','These is plural, so use are.'],'negative':'This is my friend.','bad':'This are my friend.','meaning':['متى تستخدم This is my bag؟','للإشارة إلى حقيبة قريبة مفردة','للإشارة إلى عدة حقائب بعيدة','لوصف عادة قديمة'],'context':['تقدم صديقك إلى زميل جديد. أي عبارة مناسبة؟','This is my friend, Omar.','These is my friend.','This are Omar.'],'advanced':[('This is what …','يمكن أن يأتي what-clause بعد This is لتحديد الشيء المقصود.','A what-clause can follow This is to identify the thing meant.','This is what I need.','This is ___ I need.','what',['who','where']),('The first time + present perfect','مع This is the first time يُستخدم المضارع التام عادةً للخبرة حتى الآن.','This is the first time commonly takes the present perfect for experience up to now.',"This is the first time I've been here.","This is the first time I ___ here.","have been",['am being','had been'])]},
6:{'ar':'Let’s اقتراح يشمل المتحدث والمستمع. بعده فعل أساسي دون to؛ والنفي Let’s not.','en':'Let’s makes a suggestion including the speaker and listener. Use the base verb without to; the negative is Let’s not.','tags':['اقتراح','تعاون','اجتماع','أصدقاء','suggestions'],'compare':['Let’s دعوة لفعل مشترك. Let me عرض بأن أقوم بالفعل أنا.','Let’s suggests doing something together. Let me offers for the speaker to do it.'],'gap':["Let's ___ to the park.",'go','to go','going'],'fill':["Let's ___ make the same mistake.",['not'],'يأتي not بعد Let’s للنفي.','Put not after Let’s to make a negative suggestion.'],'negative':"Let's take a break.",'bad':"Let's to take a break.",'meaning':['ماذا تقصد بـ Let’s check the map؟','اقتراح مراجعة الخريطة معًا','إجبار شخص آخر وحده','وصف فعل انتهى أمس'],'context':['تريد اقتراح استراحة على زملائك.','Let us take a break.',"Let's to take a break.",'We used to take a break.'],'advanced':[('Let’s …, shall we?','الصيغة الشائعة للسؤال الذيلي بعد Let’s هي shall we.','The usual question tag after Let’s is shall we.',"Let's begin, shall we?","Let's begin, ___?",'shall we',["do we","will you"]),('Let + object + base verb','بعد let مع مفعول يأتي فعل دون to؛ مثل let me explain.','Let + object takes the bare infinitive, as in let me explain.','Let me explain the problem.','Let me ___ the problem.','explain',['to explain','explaining'])]},
7:{'ar':'feel like بمعنى الرغبة يتبعه اسم أو فعل ينتهي بـ ing. لا تستخدم to قبل الفعل هنا.','en':'Feel like expresses a desire and is followed by a noun or an -ing form, not a to-infinitive.','tags':['مشاعر','مزاج','رغبات','وقت فراغ','feelings'],'compare':['feel like going رغبة حالية؛ want to go يستخدم to مع فعل أساسي.','Feel like going expresses a present inclination; want to go takes to + base verb.'],'gap':['I feel like ___ a book.','reading','to read','read'],'fill':['She feels like ___ at home.',['staying'],'بعد feel like يأتي staying بصيغة ing.','Use the -ing form staying after feel like.'],'negative':"I don't feel like going out.",'bad':"I don't feel like to go out.",'meaning':['ماذا تعني I feel like taking a break؟','أشعر برغبة في استراحة','أنا آخذ استراحة دائمًا منذ الطفولة','يُمنع عليّ أن أستريح'],'context':['لديك مزاج مناسب لنزهة الآن.','I feel like going for a walk.','I feel like to walk.','I feel like walked.'],'advanced':[('Feel like + noun','يمكن أن يأتي اسم بعد feel like: I feel like a coffee تعبير غير رسمي عن الرغبة في قهوة.','A noun may follow feel like: I feel like a coffee is an informal expression of desire.','I feel like a coffee.','Which is grammatical?','I feel like a coffee.',['I feel like to a coffee.','I feel like drink a coffee.']),('Different meaning: feel like + clause','feel like متبوعًا بجملة قد يصف إحساسًا أو تشبيهًا، لا مجرد رغبة في نشاط.','Feel like followed by a clause can describe a feeling or impression rather than a desire for an activity.',"I feel like I've been here before.",'Which sentence expresses an impression?',"I feel like I've been here before.",['I feel like reading a book.','I feel like a sandwich.'])]},
8:{'ar':'used to + فعل أساسي تصف عادة أو حالة سابقة تغيرت. في السؤال والنفي مع did نستخدم use to.','en':'Used to + base verb describes a past habit or state that has changed. After did or didn’t, use use to.','tags':['ماضي','عادات','ذكريات','مقارنات','past'],'compare':['used to live: كنت أعيش؛ be used to living: معتاد على العيش. في الثانية to حرف جر، وبعده ing أو اسم.','Used to live describes a former state. Be used to living means be accustomed to it; to is a preposition in the latter.'],'gap':['I used to ___ near the sea.','live','living','lived'],'fill':["Did you ___ to play football?",['use'],'في الصيغة القياسية للاختبارات نستخدم use بعد did.','In standard exam writing, use use after did.'],'negative':"I didn't use to enjoy cooking.",'bad':"I didn't used to enjoy cooking.",'meaning':['ماذا تعني I used to work here؟','كنت أعمل هنا في السابق','سأبدأ العمل هنا غدًا','أنا معتاد الآن على العمل هنا فقط'],'context':['تصف عادة سابقة لم تعد تفعلها.','I used to walk to school.',"I'm used to walking to school.",'I use walking school.'],'advanced':[('Be/get used to + -ing','مع be أو get used to يأتي اسم أو ing. هذا معنى الاعتياد، وليس تركيب العادة الماضية.','Be/get used to takes a noun or an -ing form and expresses being/becoming accustomed to something.',"I'm used to getting up early.","I'm used to ___ up early.",'getting',['get','got']),('Used to vs would','would قد يصف أفعالًا متكررة في سياق ماضٍ واضح، لكنه لا يحل عادةً محل used to في الحالات الماضية الثابتة.','Would can describe repeated actions in an established past context; it does not normally replace used to for former states.','I used to own a small shop.','Which is natural for a former state?','I used to own a small shop.',['I would own a small shop when I was young.','I use to owning a shop.'])]},
9:{'ar':'manage to + فعل أساسي تعني النجاح في الفعل، غالبًا بعد صعوبة أو جهد.','en':'Manage to + base verb means succeeding in doing something, often despite difficulty.','tags':['إنجاز','تجارب','حل مشكلات','ماضي','achievement'],'compare':['tried to تصف المحاولة ولا تضمن النجاح؛ managed to تفيد تحقق النجاح.','Tried to describes an attempt without guaranteeing success; managed to indicates success.'],'gap':['I managed to ___ on time.','finish','finishing','finished'],'fill':['She managed ___ solve the puzzle.',['to'],'manage يتبعه to-infinitive.','Manage takes a to-infinitive.'],'negative':"I didn't manage to book a ticket.",'bad':"I didn't managed to book a ticket.",'meaning':['ما الذي تفيده I managed to repair it؟','نجحت في إصلاحه','حاولت وفشلت بالضرورة','سأحاول إصلاحه غدًا'],'context':['وصلت إلى آخر قطار بعد الإسراع ونجحت في ركوبه.','I managed to catch the last train.','I tried catch the train.','I managed catching train.'],'advanced':[('Managed to vs could: one achievement','لإنجاز محدد تحقق في الماضي، managed to أو was able to أوضح عادةً من could؛ could مناسب للقدرة العامة.','For a specific successful past achievement, managed to or was able to is often clearer than could; could commonly describes general ability.','I managed to open the stuck door.','The door was stuck, but I ___ open it.','managed to',['managed','manage']),('Succeed in + -ing','تعبير قريب هو succeed in + ing؛ يختلف تركيبه عن manage to.','A related expression is succeed in + -ing, which has a different verb pattern.','She succeeded in solving the problem.','She succeeded in ___ the problem.','solving',['to solve','solve'])]},
10:{'ar':'It takes + مدة + to + فعل أساسي. يمكن إضافة الشخص: It takes me… والسؤال عن المدة How long does it take…؟','en':'Use It takes + time + to + base verb. Add an experiencer with It takes me… Ask about duration with How long does it take…?','tags':['وقت','تخطيط','سفر','عمل','time'],'compare':['takes للحاضر، took للماضي، will take للمستقبل. لا نخلط take مع spend الذي يأخذ شخصًا فاعلًا وing غالبًا.','Use takes for the present, took for the past, and will take for the future. Spend normally has a person as subject and an -ing complement.'],'gap':['It ___ ten minutes to get there.','takes','take','taking'],'fill':['How long does it ___ to get there?',['take'],'بعد does يعود الفعل إلى الصيغة الأساسية take.','After does, use the base form take.'],'negative':"It doesn't take long to make this meal.",'bad':"It doesn't takes long to make this meal.",'meaning':['ما السؤال المناسب للاستفسار عن مدة رحلة؟','How long does it take?','How many does it takes?','What long it take?'],'context':['تخبر زميلك أن إنهاء المهمة استغرق ثلاث ساعات أمس.','It took three hours to finish the job.','It takes three hours yesterday.','It taking three hours.'],'advanced':[('Take vs spend','It took me an hour to write it تساوي في المعنى I spent an hour writing it مع اختلاف البناء.','It took me an hour to write it and I spent an hour writing it describe the same duration with different structures.','I spent an hour writing the report.','I spent an hour ___ the report.','writing',['to write','write']),('Take + effort or qualities','قد يأتي بعد takes اسم مثل patience أو courage بدل مدة زمنية.','Takes can be followed by a required quality or effort, such as patience or courage.','It takes courage to speak in public.','It takes courage ___ in public.','to speak',['speaking','speak'])]},
11:{'ar':'worth يتبعها اسم أو فعل ing. لا نستخدم worth to do. الصفة تصف قيمة تستحق الجهد.','en':'Worth is followed by a noun or an -ing form, not a to-infinitive. It describes value that justifies effort.','tags':['اختيارات','تقييم','قرارات','رأي','value'],'compare':['worth doing؛ أما worthwhile فيمكن أن يأتي في It is worthwhile to do something أو doing something.','Use worth doing. Worthwhile can occur in It is worthwhile to do something or doing something.'],'gap':["It's worth ___ again.",'trying','to try','try'],'fill':['This book is worth ___ twice.',['reading'],'بعد worth نستخدم reading، دون to.','Use reading after worth, without to.'],'negative':"It isn't worth arguing about.",'bad':"It isn't worth to argue about.",'meaning':['ماذا تعني It’s worth checking؟','التحقق منه يستحق الجهد','يحظر التحقق منه','تم التحقق منه بالفعل بالضرورة'],'context':['متحف جميل وتوصي بزيارته.','The museum is worth visiting.','The museum is worth to visit.','The museum worth visit.'],'advanced':[('Worth with passive meaning','This book is worth reading تعني أن قراءة الكتاب مفيدة؛ لا نضيف being read في هذا الاستعمال المعتاد.','This book is worth reading has an understood passive relationship: the book is the thing people read.','The book is worth reading.','The book is worth ___.','reading',['to read','read']),('Worth + noun phrase','يمكن أن يتبع worth اسم يعبّر عن الجهد أو المال، مثل worth the wait أو worth ten pounds.','Worth can take a noun phrase for effort or monetary value, such as worth the wait or worth ten pounds.','The view was worth the long walk.','Which is grammatical?','The view was worth the long walk.',['The view was worth to the walk.','The view was worth walk to.'])]},
12:{'ar':'داخل السؤال غير المباشر نستخدم ترتيب الخبر: الفاعل ثم الفعل. لا نكرر قلب السؤال بعد where أو when أو if.','en':'Inside an indirect question, use statement word order: subject before verb. Do not repeat question inversion after where, when, or if.','tags':['أسئلة','اتجاهات','تهذيب','اختبارات','questions'],'compare':['Where is the station? سؤال مباشر؛ Do you know where the station is? سؤال غير مباشر.','Where is the station? is direct. Do you know where the station is? contains an indirect question.'],'gap':['Do you know where the station ___?','is','does','are'],'fill':['Do you know where she ___?',['works'],'داخل السؤال المضمن نستخدم she works دون does.','Use statement order she works inside the embedded question, without does.'],'negative':"I don't know where he went.",'bad':"I don't know where did he go.",'meaning':['أي صيغة مناسبة لسؤال غير مباشر عن المكان؟','Do you know where she lives?','Do you know where does she live?','Do you know where lives she?'],'context':['تريد أن تسأل بأدب إن كانت المكتبة مفتوحة.','Do you know if the library is open?','Do you know is the library open?','Do you know if is the library open?'],'advanced':[('Subject questions','عندما تكون what أو who هي الفاعل، كما في what happened، لا نضيف did. هذا ليس استثناءً عشوائيًا من ترتيب الخبر.','When what or who is the subject, as in what happened, do not add did. The embedded clause still has its normal subject-verb structure.','Do you know what happened?','Do you know what ___?','happened',['did happened','does happened']),('If/whether clauses','لإدراج سؤال إجابته نعم أو لا نستخدم if أو whether مع ترتيب الخبر.','Use if or whether to embed a yes/no question, with statement word order.','Could you tell me whether the train is late?','Could you tell me ___ the train is late?','whether',['what','where'])]}}

